        {
            "block_label": "doc_title",
            "block_content": "Part 8-In-house asset rules applying to regulated  superannuation funds ",
            "block_bbox": [
                171,
                180,
                1011,
                253
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Division 1-Object and interpretation ",
            "block_bbox": [
                168,
                287,
                734,
                318
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "Subdivision A-General ",
            "block_bbox": [
                166,
                345,
                504,
                370
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "69 Object of Part ",
            "block_bbox": [
                165,
                407,
                397,
                434
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The object of this Part is to set out rules about the level of the in-house assets of regulated superannuation funds.",
            "block_bbox": [
                303,
                461,
                990,
                516
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "69A Sub-funds to be treated as funds.",
            "block_bbox": [
                163,
                552,
                645,
                578
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A sub-fund within a regulated superannuation fund is taken for the purposes of this Part to be a regulated superannuation fund if the sub-fund satisfies the following conditions:",
            "block_bbox": [
                300,
                608,
                1045,
                692
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(a) the sub-fund has separately identifiable assets and separately identifiable beneficiaries; and ",
            "block_bbox": [
                319,
                704,
                1042,
                755
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(b) the interest of each beneficiary of the sub-fund is determined by reference only to the conditions governing that sub-fund.",
            "block_bbox": [
                318,
                766,
                1043,
                820
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "70A The Regulator may determine a person to be a standard employer-sponsor \n",
            "block_bbox": [
                159,
                857,
                949,
                914
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(1) For the purposes of this Part, the Regulator may determine in writing that a person, who is not a standard employer-sponsor of a regulated superannuation fund within the meaning of subsection 16(2), is taken to be a standard employer-sponsor of the fund.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                253,
                939,
                1044,
                1079
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "(2) If the Regulator makes a determination under subsection (1) or revokes a determination so made, the Regulator must as soon as practicable after making or revoking the determination, inform a trustee of the regulated superannuation fund concerned, in writing,of the making or revocation of the determination.",
            "block_bbox": [
                253,
                1106,
                1023,
                1244
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "footer",
            "block_content": "Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993",
            "block_bbox": [
                441,
